From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:00:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): keep local obligation path and bind historical
 selfwork repair [daveey]

Problem: independent review of #3743 at a60ab8d2 requested changes: a
same-gateway creator with an accepted obligation was refused, and historical
repair authorized a never-holder after journaling a stale unauthorized refusal.

Why 1: receive() sent every creator.gateway==origin.gateway request to
_local_proof and never consulted _obligation.
Why 2: a worker on a chat-created local card has owner_admitted session !=
origin.session, so local proof fails while an accepted same-gateway obligation
would have authorized it on base.
Why 3: historical repair skipped the lease and treated any matching
self_work_creator_unauthorized journal row as proof, including a correct
stale/spoof refusal.
Root (happened): the local-origin split was by gateway equality, not by whether
an accepted obligation existed; repair authenticated the envelope, not that
this sender held the run while that refusal was live.
Root (not caught): tests covered live local detectors and remote obligations
separately, not same-gateway obligation plus never-holder/stale-journal repair.
Recurrence: first review of this PR (review 5988263187).

Countermeasures:
- try an accepted obligation first for every creator, including local; keep
  live local proof when no obligation exists
- historical same-id repair requires the latest claimed holder == sender and
  the journaled refusal timestamp while that run was live
- BEGIN IMMEDIATE rechecks the same branch

Proof: RED then GREEN in tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_selfwork_forward.py
(60 passed); 16 selfwork consumer files 404 passed; scripts/check --base
origin/main 21 ok.

Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.6 <noreply@x.ai>
